   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize the village of New Berlin, in the county of Chenango, to discontinue the use of certain lands as parklands",
    "basePrintNo": "A8774",
    "basePrintNoStr": "A8774-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Parks",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:A8774\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to authorize the village of New Berlin, in the\ncounty of Chenango, to discontinue the use of certain lands as parklands\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nTo authorize the village of New Berlin to discontinue the use of certain\nparklands.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nSection 1. Subject to the provisions of this act, the village of New\nBerlin, in the county of Chenango, acting by and through its board of\ntrustees, is hereby authorized to discontinue as parklands and alienate,\nsell and convey for fair market value, fee simple title to the lands\ndescribed in section three of this act.\n\nSection 2. The authorization contained in section one of this act shall\ntake effect only upon the condition that the village of New Berlin dedi-\ncate all proceeds from the sale of the premises described in section\nthree of this act for making capital improvements to park facilities in\nthe village and, in addition, the village of New Berlin shall dedicate\nthe lands described in section four of this act as additional parklands\nof the village.\n\nSection 3. The lands authorized by section one of this act to be discon-\ntinued as parklands are as follows on the bill (see bill).\n\nSection 4. The replacement lands to be dedicated by the village of New\nBerlin, Chenango county to use as parkland for public park purposes are\nlocated in the town of New Berlin, Chenango county comprise a total\n16.496 acres or more or less and particularly described as follows (see\nbill, Section 4 Parcel I, II, III).\n\nSection 5. The discontinuance and conveyance of parkland authorized by\nthe provisions of this act shall not occur until the village of New\nBerlin has complied with federal requirements pertaining to the alien-\nation or conversion of parklands, including satisfying the secretary of\nthe interior that the alienation or conversion complies with all condi-\ntions which the secretary of the interior deems necessary to assure the\nsubstitution of other lands shall be equivalent in fair market value and\nrecreational usefulness to the lands being alienated or converted.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThe Village of New Berlin resolved to consolidate its recreation\nfacilities/athletic fields with a multi-purpose park adjacent to the\nTown's Merritt (Doc) Meyers Memorial Park on County Route 29. The\ncurrent playing field located above the old New Berlin Central School\nbuilding will be sold to the private educational facility of Milford\nAcademy. The Village of New Berlin has determined that the Academy is\nbest suited to handle this property and to create a capital fund to\ndevelop a larger, more all purpose village park that would better bene-\nfit the residents of the village and larger community and this will\n\nconsolidate the Village/Town recreation facilities in a convenient\nlocation with plenty of parking and facilities available for all ages.\n\nThe Village of New Berlin and the Town of New Berlin have agreed to\nprovide the playing fields for the Village of New Berlin's youth\nprograms. This agreement insures continuity of the use of the field to\nbe replaced. This legislation will discontinue the use of Fish Field and\nthe proceeds will create a capital fund to start community planning of a\nbetter facility.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nTo be determined.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
